cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "hydroml: a configuration-driven template for machine-learning hydrological modelling"
abstract: >-
  A template for streamflow simulation from sub-basin precipitation and
  temperature. Data-driven travel-time (lag) selection per sub-basin,
  chronological train/validation/test splitting, 17 regression models compared
  under one protocol, hyper-parameter search with refinement, time-series
  cross-validation, and projection of a trained model onto climate scenarios.
  A new case study requires editing a YAML configuration file only.
